:answer/id #uuid "5121b2ec-f55e-536b-9787-5bf44f6de907" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186333730} :answer-field/id #uuid "39aaac3a-a375-54e9-93b9-3f8aae2090b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335350}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f32325ca-f6af-5642-b811-5b2d78cf8877" :question/math-academy-id "q-66594" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{3},$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x-5\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-5)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{3},$ we get that $tan⁡(x-5\\pi )=\\sqrt{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338869 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37934bed-1f9a-50c5-9a8d-e5b0b59e71a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336549} {:answer/id #uuid "4b39580e-c808-5289-b894-51d8505df304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336729} {:answer/id #uuid "5de9a8b6-2bf6-5e41-98c3-3ffaa96e81dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336881} {:answer/id #uuid "81ac5deb-9cc0-5543-8625-93f7cbf3fed8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337211} {:answer/id #uuid "b2061940-30fc-5eef-a2d6-609b6aeedec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b2061940-30fc-5eef-a2d6-609b6aeedec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337622} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ab98c3a-7c21-528d-8351-dfb2882c1ded" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338295}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "35b95266-3a2f-569f-acd3-81fb0b0052f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-70998" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=3,$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=5$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+5\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x+5\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=3,$ we get that $tan⁡(x+5\\pi )=3.$\n\nFinally, then\n\n$$\ntan⁡(x+5\\pi )+2=(3)+2=5.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2483a9ae-953e-586e-b9ea-aa4eddbc58be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336373} {:answer/id #uuid "38fa474b-0c10-5a11-8790-80e7d2ccd89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336567} {:answer/id #uuid "58b1ef3d-0461-54d4-bfef-0dcf4e47f62f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336843} {:answer/id #uuid "7a68b43d-b00e-5755-83a4-9a7442c7cd27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}-11\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337134} {:answer/id #uuid "cb68ac70-7dcf-5366-bb7d-8472a8b471b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb68ac70-7dcf-5366-bb7d-8472a8b471b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337819} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae78200b-d5d2-5ea6-ac9b-8cafbca6c0e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338598}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "382314ca-5ab1-5780-bf33-5145bcded9fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-71002" :question/problem "If $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ for some $x$, find the value of $tan⁡(x-11\\pi ).$" :question/worked-solution "The period of $y=tan⁡x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for integer $n$ we have\n\n$$\ntan⁡x=tan⁡(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-11$ into the right-hand-side of the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡x=tan⁡(x+(-11)\\cdot \\pi )=tan⁡(x-11\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $tan⁡x=\\sqrt{2},$ we get that $tan⁡(x-11\\pi )=\\sqrt{2}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Utilizing the Periodicity Property of the Tangent Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175699 :question/id #uuid "12dc1c50-69bc-54d8-8d60-a7fc144c9644" :question/math-academy-id "e-11008" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the graph of $y=\\csc x?$\n\n- The function takes the value $1$ at $x = -\\dfrac {\\pi} 2 + 2 \\pi n,$ where $n$ is an integer\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty,+\\infty)$\n\n- The function has zeroes at $x = 0, \\pm \\pi, \\pm 2 \\pi,\\dots$" :question/worked-solution "Let's have a look at the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/a9/a92d46319d381f0a8cab7823021b3b7e9b5c030ad964586b8e72129a2cd5abe7.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x = \\dfrac {\\pi} 2 + 2 \\pi n.$ Therefore, statement I is false.\n\n- The range of $y = \\csc x$ is $(-\\infty,-1] \\cup [1, \\infty).$ Therefore, statement II is false.\n\n- The cosecant graph does not intersect the $x$-axis. Therefore, statement III is false.\n\nIn conclusion, none of the statements are true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049075 :topic/math-academy-id 1573 :topic/title "Graphing Secant and Cosecant"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050172 :topic/math-academy-id 3540 :topic/title "Describing Properties of the Sine Function"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176487 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a4d9a5b4-143b-5f70-96af-c54653decc87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175061} {:answer/id #uuid "bc66d19e-5e0e-5472-94a8-e7027abf7aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175062} {:answer/id #uuid "d19b760d-4b8d-5e73-9344-5302538b3f30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175063} {:answer/id #uuid "d982c693-68ac-55c9-a06f-bf9fdb410dce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175064} {:answer/id #uuid "0d82be89-281b-59c1-8ba2-fc6631fb56f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175065}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f4ea36c4-9c29-57d9-8e19-0b623c6933dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175060}] :question/id #uuid "5961bc49-07f6-5191-b949-28358553d498" :question/math-academy-id "q-42912" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y = \\csc x$? Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\n1. The point $(π,-1)$ is not on the graph.\n2. The function has a vertical asymptotes at $x = nπ$.\n3. The value $y = 2$ is in the range of the function."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176548 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c602a5b-2bb3-53e8-8c57-c44d7943c842" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175427} {:answer/id #uuid "94423566-84d6-59e2-b948-35feec5648f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186175428} {:answer/id #uu